[?25l[0m[38;5;141m> [0m[38;5;252m[1m## What was wrong and what I changed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two bugs in [38;5;10mtranslated_rust/src/hash_blake.rs[0m:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### Bug 1: Missing C ABI export symbol[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The test runner dynamically loads the shared library and looks up [38;5;10mSPX_hash_message[0m (the C code uses [38;5;10m#define hash_message SPX_NAMESPACE(hash_message)[0m which expands to [38;5;10mSPX_hash_message[0m). The Rust translation only had an internal [38;5;10mpub fn hash_message(...)[0m with no [38;5;10m#[no_mangle] extern "C"[0m wrapper using the [38;5;10mSPX_[0m prefixed name.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mFix:[22m Added a [38;5;10m#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub extern "C" fn SPX_hash_message(...)[0m wrapper that converts raw pointers to slices and delegates to the internal [38;5;10mhash_message[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### Bug 2: Incorrect bit-length conversion in blake512_update calls[0m[0m
[0m[0m
This is the subtle one. The C [38;5;10mblake512_update[0m function takes [38;5;10mdatalen[0m in [1mbits[22m (it does [38;5;10mleft = S->buflen >> 3[0m to convert to bytes internally). However, the C [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m and [38;5;10mhash_message[0m functions pass [1mbyte counts[22m directly:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mc
[0m[38;5;10mblakeX_update(&S, R, SPX_N);        // SPX_N = 24 (bytes, but treated as bits)
blakeX_update(&S, pk, SPX_PK_BYTES); // 48 (bytes, but treated as bits)
blakeX_update(&S, m, mlen);          // mlen in bytes, treated as bits
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust translator "helpfully" multiplied by 8 to convert bytes→bits:[0m[0m
[1mrust
[0m[38;5;10mblake512_update(&mut s, &r[..SPX_N], (SPX_N as u64) * 8);  // 192 bits
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
But this changes the behavior — the C code passes 24 (meaning 3 bytes get hashed), while the Rust was passing 192 (meaning 24 bytes get hashed). The test vectors were generated from the C code, so the Rust must match the C behavior exactly.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mFix:[22m Removed all [38;5;10m* 8[0m multiplications in both [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m and [38;5;10mhash_message[0m, passing the raw byte counts just like the C code does.[0m[0m
